--- a/packages/native-client-rust/FEATURES.md
+++ b/packages/native-client-rust/FEATURES.md
@@ -227,3 +227,44 @@ writer cleanup and profile recovery remain separate from phone receipt.
 Synthetic equality, commit, fault, restart and disconnected-session fixtures do
 not establish a live latency or recipient-validation result. New comparison and
 proof timing phases are nested in their parent phases and must not be added twice.
+
+### Native background WAL checkpoints
+
+Native Core enables owned account-control checkpoint maintenance after its local
+startup recovery. Standalone Stores, Simulator Core and DELETE-mode connections
+keep the ordinary inline policy. FULL WAL commits still finish before receipt
+parsing or final send acceptance; background maintenance does not grant a new
+network attempt or replace an accepted send receipt.
+
+Maintenance uses a separately admitted connection under the same Store ownership
+lease. Ordinary due work waits for 100ms without control activity on that account;
+read control calls count as activity, but the maintenance health view does not.
+The original frame, pending-age and free-space pressure bounds bypass that delay,
+while retaining foreground exclusion and complete family admission. Other accounts
+and work outside control calls are not a global disk-idle signal. A checkpoint
+already started may still compete with later work for the same disk.
+Its PASSIVE checkpoint IO holds no account, registry or admitted-writer
+mutex. Controlled family epochs preserve current writer identity, exact companion
+membership and private permissions during overlap, then return to full metadata
+admission checks. Removal, eviction, shutdown and uncertain-family cleanup retain
+their ownership and stale-generation guards. Checkpoint pressure or failure is
+maintenance health, not permission to regenerate or resend a completed reply.
+Only the maintenance `blocked` result gates a new remote admission; an ordinary
+checkpoint error alone does not invalidate later FULL commits. An existing
+idempotent reply remains available, and a blocked queued text or quoted reply
+keeps its saved task without claiming it. Results already in flight keep their
+original receipt and completion paths. Sync and metadata APIs check storage
+pressure before creating a new operation. Already-created sync and metadata
+operations keep their existing failure and recovery behavior; this change adds
+no new operation resumer or retry policy.
+
+`GET /v1/accounts/{accountId}/storage-maintenance` requires that account's `read`
+scope and returns maintenance state without reading its control database or
+official profile. Ordinary account status also includes `checkpointMaintenance`;
+the separate endpoint remains usable if those other account reads fail. Shutdown
+signals maintenance without waiting under account locks. The server's owner guard
+joins maintenance on successful or failed serve exits even when another worker
+still retains Core; it leaves in-flight SQLite handles open. Store destruction
+closes handles before releasing ownership. Read snapshots use the live health view
+without owning or stopping a second worker. Timing and fault fixtures do not
+establish phone delivery or a measured end-to-end latency improvement.
